            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0282" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00/1110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schuyler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-14T12:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1921—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 8:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Salvadorean Government considers international status of three states of the
                    union unchanged and that foreign relations continue as before until the meeting
                    of the Federal Council next February when it will ask for recognition, first
                    from us, afterwards from the other powers. Above repeated to Guatemala and
                    Honduras.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
